<h2>Carrollton properties and common claims</h2>
<h3>Homes and townhomes</h3>
<p>Carrollton's housing ranges from brick ranch homes in older neighborhoods to two-story homes and townhomes in newer areas. Hail of the size recorded here can crack shingles, dent gutters and garage doors, shred screens, and damage siding and fencing. Steeper, more complex roofs on newer homes mean higher repair costs that should be reflected in the estimate. Our <a href="/services/hail-damage-claims/">hail damage claims</a> and <a href="/services/roof-damage-insurance-claims/">roof damage claims</a> pages explain what to document.</p>
<h3>Warehouses and commercial buildings</h3>
<p>Industrial and office properties along I-35E and Belt Line Rd. often have low-slope TPO or modified-bitumen roofs, metal panels, rooftop HVAC units, and large overhead doors. Wind can peel roof membranes and panels, and hail can bruise roofing and dent mechanical units in ways that are hard to see from the ground. Learn about <a href="/services/commercial-property-claims/">commercial property claims</a>.</p>
<h3>Water and flooding</h3>
<p>Wind-driven rain through damaged roofs often leads to interior <a href="/services/water-damage-claims/">water damage</a>. Flash flooding near creeks and low crossings is a different matter: standard homeowners and commercial policies generally exclude flood, which is covered by NFIP or private flood policies.</p>

